17106,"We need to translate the Arabic text into Urdu, output only the translation, no intro, explanation, quotes, or notes. The Arabic text includes parentheses and numbers, but we need to translate the content. The text is a chain of narrators (isnad) and hadith). We need to translate it into Urdu preserving the meaning, but not adding any extra commentary. Should we keep the Arabic terms? Usually translation would render into Urdu language, possibly keeping proper nouns transliterated. The instruction: ""Translate the following complete Arabic Hadith text into Urdu. Output ONLY the translated text in Urdu, do not include any intro, explanation, quotes, or notes"". So we need to produce Urdu translation of the given Arabic passage.We need to translate the Arabic sentences, including the chain of narrators and the statement about the hadith. Let's parse the Arabic:(۱۷۱۰۰) وَرَوَاہُ ابْنُ عُیَیْنَۃَ کَمَا حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو الْحَسَنِ : مُحَمَّدُ بْنُ الْحُسَیْنِ الْعَلَوِیُّ إِمْلاَئً أَخْبَرَنَا حَاجِبُ بْنُ أَحْمَدَ حَدَّثَنَا عَبْدُ الرَّحِیمِ بْنُ مُنِیبٍ حَدَّثَنَا سُفْیَانُ (ح) وَأَخْبَرَنَا أَبُو سَعِیدِ بْنُ أَبِی عَمْرٍو حَدَّثَنَا أَبُو الْعَبَّاسِ الأَصَمُّ أَخْبَرَنَا الرَّبِیعُ قَالَ قَالَ الشَّافِعِیُّ أَخْبَرَنَا ابْنُ عُیَیْنَۃَ (ح) وَأَخْبَرَنَا أَبُو الْحُسَیْنِ بْنُ الْفَضْلِ الْقَطَّانُ بِبَغْدَادَ أَخْبَرَنَا عَبْدُ اللَّہِ بْنُ جَعْفَرِ بْنِ دُرُسْتُوَ"
